# Clients (by rDNS hostname suffix, IP, or CIDR) to always allow through
# greylisting immediately. One entry per line; see postgrey-whitelist-clients(5).
#
# This is the .local companion of /etc/postgrey/whitelist_clients — the
# large list maintained by the postgrey Debian package. Postgrey reads both;
# put your own additions here so package upgrades never touch them.
#
# Ulaknode additions: transactional ESPs that carry one-time codes and
# password-reset mail, where a greylisting delay hurts most. Entries match
# the connecting client's reverse-DNS name suffix.
amazonses.com
sendgrid.net
mailgun.org
mailgun.net
sparkpostmail.com
mtasv.net
protection.outlook.com
mandrillapp.com
mcsv.net
rsgsv.net
